Also note that this kind of test usually involves multiple runs or more complex execution, therefore you might want to rerun these tests after each modification in order to ensure that your code still behaves as expected for any incoming input. 
This kind of test can give you strong confidence in your code, but it won't replace simple unit testing or regression testing, which is also essential as your project grows and new features are added. 
Also remember that testing with tools like PeX doesn't replace a good unit test or a manual test, but it can be helpful to automate some parts of the testing or to find edge cases where unit tests might be hard to find.

